---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { loadIndex, loadTraceStore } from "../../lib/catalog";
import { TACTIC_LABEL, incidentSlug, loadCandidates, loadIncidents, loadSourceCheck, machineReviewed } from "../../lib/incidents";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
const index = loadIndex();
const records = index?.records ?? [];
const total = records.length;
const withTrace = records.filter((r) => (r.trust.traces ?? 5) < 5).length;
const store = loadTraceStore();
const asOf = index?.built_at ? index.built_at.slice(0, 10) : "the last build";

const set = loadIncidents();
const incidents = set?.incidents ?? [];
const tacticsUsed = [...new Set(incidents.flatMap((i) => i.tactics ?? []))].sort();
const cands = loadCandidates();
const candidatesUrl = "https://github.com/Sushegaad/AgentDossier/blob/main/data/curated/incident_candidates.yaml";
const check = loadSourceCheck();
const attention = new Set(check?.needs_attention ?? []);
const machine = incidents.filter(machineReviewed).length;
---

<Base title="Traces" description="Public traces of AI agents attacking or defending systems — an incident registry with tactics, timelines and sources.">
  <div class="prose" style="max-width: 100%">
    <div class="eyebrow muted" style="color: var(--accent-ink)">Public traces</div>
    <h1 style="font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 5vw, 3.4rem); max-width: 18ch; line-height: 1.05">Agents attacking and defending, on record</h1>
    <p class="body" style="max-width: 72ch">
      The public traces of AI agents attacking or defending systems that this registry has found and
      curated from post-mortems, advisories, filings and the press. Each row is one incident — open it
      for the timeline, what defenders can take from it, the tactics and the sources. "Defenders can't
      learn from what they can't see," so this is the record so far, and
      <a href={`${base}/methodology/#traces`}>how it is collected</a>.
    </p>

    <div class="row" style="gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; margin: 18px 0 10px">
      <span class="tiny muted">
        {incidents.length} incident{incidents.length === 1 ? "" : "s"} · {tacticsUsed.length} tactics · as of {set?.collected_on ?? asOf}
        {cands && cands.scoutedOn && <> · {cands.sourcesChecked} feeds scouted {cands.scoutedOn}</>}
        {cands?.reviewedOn && <> · machine-reviewed {cands.reviewedOn}</>}
        {machine > 0 && <> · {machine} of {incidents.length} rows published by the weekly review</>}
      </span>
      <a class="btn small" href={`${base}/traces/export.json`} style="margin-left: auto">Export registry (JSON)</a>
    </div>

    <div class="scroll-x" tabindex="0">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>ID</th>
            <th>Incident</th>
            <th>AI role</th>
            <th>Attacker</th>
            <th>Defender</th>
            <th>Tactics</th>
            <th>Sources</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {incidents.map((inc) => (
            <tr>
              <td style="white-space: nowrap; font-weight: 800"><a href={`${base}/traces/${incidentSlug(inc.id)}/`} style="color: var(--ink)">{inc.id}</a><div class="tiny muted">{inc.date}</div></td>
              <td>
                <a href={`${base}/traces/${incidentSlug(inc.id)}/`} style="font-weight: 700; color: var(--ink)">{inc.title}</a>
                {inc.window && <div class="tiny muted">{inc.window}</div>}
              </td>
              <td class="small">{inc.ai_role}</td>
              <td class="small">{inc.attacker.description}</td>
              <td class="small">{inc.defender.description}</td>
              <td class="tiny" style="white-space: nowrap">{(inc.tactics ?? []).join(" · ") || "—"}</td>
              <td class="small">{inc.sources.length}{machineReviewed(inc) ? <div class="tiny muted">machine-reviewed</div> : inc.reviewer ? "" : <div class="tiny muted">unreviewed</div>}{attention.has(inc.id) && <div class="tiny" style="color: var(--danger)" title="a source link moved or no longer answers">⚠ source link</div>}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="tiny muted" style="margin-top: 10px">
      {tacticsUsed.map((t) => `${t} ${TACTIC_LABEL[t] ?? ""}`).join(" · ")} (MITRE ATT&CK). Compiled from the linked public sources, as reported — not attributions, findings of fault or legal conclusions. Rows marked <em>machine-reviewed</em> were read and published by the weekly review ({cands?.reviewedBy ?? "a model"}) from their sources, with every decision on record; the first rows were written by hand.{check && <> Source links re-checked {check.checked_on}: {check.summary.ok} of {check.sources_checked} answer{attention.size ? `; ${attention.size} flagged below` : ""}.</>}
    </p>

    <section style="border-top: 2px solid var(--rule); margin-top: 40px; padding-top: 20px; max-width: 76ch">
      <h2>Across the catalog</h2>
      <p class="body">
        Beyond these incidents, every agent dossier says whether <em>anyone</em> has watched that
        agent under attack — and for most the honest answer is "none found." That coverage is the
        other half of the gap.
      </p>
      <div class="stats" style="margin: 16px 0">
        <div class="stat"><div class="n">{withTrace}</div><div class="l">of {total} agents with a public trace</div></div>
        <div class="stat"><div class="n">{total - withTrace}</div><div class="l">with none found</div></div>
        <div class="stat"><div class="n">{store.length}</div><div class="l">probe & benchmark bundles in the store</div></div>
      </div>
      <h3>Where the record comes from</h3>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>This registry</strong> — the incidents above, curated from public reports (<code>data/curated/incidents.yaml</code>). A weekly <strong>scout</strong> reads {cands?.sourcesChecked || "a list of"} public feeds (press, researcher labs, vendor advisories) and keeps anything that names both an agent and an attack as a <a href={candidatesUrl} rel="noopener">candidate</a>; a weekly <strong>machine review</strong> then reads each candidate's source and publishes it when it describes a specific, real event — or dismisses it with the reason on file. No one waits on a person; <a href={`${base}/methodology/#traces`}>the bar it has to clear</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Agent-level traces</strong> on each dossier — curated write-ups, the registry's own reproducible endpoint probes (hash-chained, <code>data/traces/</code>), and harness runs against the AgentDojo prompt-injection benchmark.</li>
        <li><strong>Vendor-published bundles</strong> declared in an ARD manifest, fetched and hash-checked (<a href="https://github.com/Sushegaad/AgentDossier/blob/main/docs/traces-spec.md" rel="noopener">publishing spec</a>).</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="tiny muted">
        The store (<code>data/traces/index.jsonl</code>) is append-only and hash-chained; CI verifies it on every change. Behaviour is published, never weapons: scenario inputs and the agent's actions, no payloads against third-party systems.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
